Package: cpmemu
Architecture: any
Suggests:
 cpmemu-doc,
Description: CP/M 2.2 emulator that runs CP/M programs on the host
 cpmemu runs CP/M 2.2 .COM programs on Linux.  It emulates a Z80 or an 8080
 CPU, and it answers the BDOS and BIOS calls of the program on the host.
 Each CP/M drive is a host directory, and each CP/M file is a host file, so
 CP/M programs such as compilers, assemblers and BASIC interpreters work on
 host files directly.  No CP/M system image and no ROM are needed.
 .
 Text files can be converted between CP/M CR LF line ends and host line ends
 as the program reads and writes them.  Redirected input and output work, so
 CP/M tools can run in scripts and builds.  A GDB remote stub allows
 debugging of the CP/M program.
 .
 The package also contains cpm_disk, which makes CP/M disk images (8-inch
 SSSD floppies, and the RomWBW hd1k and combo hard disk formats) and copies
 files into and out of them.

Package: cpmemu-doc
Section: doc
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: CP/M 2.2 emulator that runs CP/M programs on the host - documentation
 cpmemu runs CP/M 2.2 .COM programs on Linux.  It emulates a Z80 or an 8080
 CPU, and it answers the BDOS and BIOS calls of the program on the host.
 .
 This package contains the documentation of cpmemu and cpm_disk, in
 Markdown: how to run CP/M programs, the configuration file, the console,
 the GDB stub, the disk image formats and the test suite.  It also contains
 example configuration files.
